{"id": "amendment-ba25df11", "type": "amendment", "question": "What change did the Finance Act, 2026 make to section 275(4)(a), and what did the provision say before the amendment?", "metrics": {"recall@1": 1.0, "hit@1": 1.0, "recall@5": 1.0, "hit@5": 1.0, "recall@10": 1.0, "hit@10": 1.0, "mrr": 1.0, "refused": 0.0, "should_refuse": 0.0, "fact_recall": 1.0, "all_facts": 1.0, "fact_recall_exact": 1.0, "all_facts_exact": 1.0, "citation_precision": 1.0, "citation_recall": 1.0, "grounded_numbers": 1.0, "amendment_type": 1.0, "prior_text_f1": 0.550561797752809}, "retrieved": [{"chunk_id": "v2:s275(4)", "provisions": ["s275(4)", "s275(4)(a)", "s275(4)(a)(i)", "s275(4)(a)(ii)", "s275(4)(b)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:preamble", "provisions": ["preamble"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s275(16)", "provisions": ["s275(16)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s267(9)", "provisions": ["s267(9)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s274(12)", "provisions": ["s274(12)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s275(1)", "provisions": ["s275(1)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s275(18)", "provisions": ["s275(18)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s1", "provisions": ["s1", "s1(1)", "s1(2)", "s1(3)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s275(7)", "provisions": ["s275(7)", "s275(7)(a)", "s275(7)(b)"]}, {"chunk_id": "v2:s275(19)", "provisions": ["s275(19)"]}], "jina_tokens": 0, "evidence_tokens": 1166, "latency_s": 1.21, "llm_tokens": 1957, "answer": "The Finance Act, 2026 substituted the wording of sub‑section (4)(a) of section 275. Before the amendment sub‑section (4) read: “(4) The Assessing Officer shall, irrespective of anything contained in section 286, pass the assessment order under sub‑section (3) within one month from the end of the month in which,— (a) the acceptance is received; or (b) the period of filing of objections under sub‑section (2) expires.” After the amendment the provision was changed to read: “(4) (a) [The Assessing Officer shall, irrespective of anything contained in section 286, pass the assessment order under sub‑section (3) within one month from the end of the month in which,— (i) the acceptance is received; or (ii) the period of filing of objections under sub‑section (2) expires.]”", "refused": false, "cited": ["v2:s275(4)"]}
